  "leg_text": "AIRBORNE B. The DARK FAR thigh swings FORWARD to screen RIGHT: its dark knee is clearly in front of its own hip and raised. The dark shin folds BACK under that raised dark knee; the dark foot is curled in the air. The WHITE NEAR thigh extends BACK to screen LEFT; its white knee and ankle both trail behind its own hip, with the white boot curled and pointing down/back in the air. BOTH complete boots are above the ground. Keep the entire WHITE NEAR leg behind and the entire DARK FAR thigh ahead. Do not put a bright thigh at the forward knee, and do not merely darken an old front leg.",
